WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.280
Mank?

00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:12.718
It's Orson Welles.

00:00:13.836 --> 00:00:15.397
Of course it is.

00:00:16.162 --> 00:00:18.208
I think it's time we talked.

00:00:18.282 --> 00:00:20.164
What is it the writer says?

00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:22.120
"Tell the story you know."

00:00:26.077 --> 00:00:27.247
Hello, everyone.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:29.200
Make yourself to home, Mr. Mankiewicz.

00:00:29.292 --> 00:00:30.315
Or shall I call you Herman?

00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:32.702
-Please, call me Mank.
-Mank.

00:00:32.786 --> 00:00:34.417
-Mank.
-Mank.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.494
This is Herman Mankiewicz,
but we have to call him Mank.

00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:38.792
Mankiewicz?

00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:40.376
Herman Mankiewicz,

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.482
New York playwright and drama critic?

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.024
Turned humble screenwriter. Mr. Hearst.

00:00:45.107 --> 00:00:49.001
This is a business where the buyer
gets nothing for his money but a memory.

00:00:49.084 --> 00:00:51.800
What he bought
still belongs to the man who sold it.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.638
-That's the real magic of the movies.
-Action!

00:00:53.718 --> 00:00:55.227
Thunder, lightning, blood,

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.560
fire, religion...

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.878
Help! Someone save me!

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.457
All in one film?

00:01:00.542 --> 00:01:01.958
That's director-proof.

00:01:02.042 --> 00:01:04.350
That's why I always want Mank around.

00:01:05.528 --> 00:01:08.225
I hear you're hunting dangerous game.

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.913
God bless William Randolph Hearst.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.708
Ready and willing
to hunt the great white whale?

00:01:14.792 --> 00:01:16.198
Just call me Ahab.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.277
-Do come in.
-At this rate, you'll never finish.

00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:24.125
You said 90 days. Welles said 60.
I'm doing the best I can.

00:01:24.212 --> 00:01:27.479
I've put up with your suicidal drinking,
your compulsive gambling,

00:01:27.542 --> 00:01:29.157
your silly platonic affairs.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.092
You owe me, Herman.

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:33.558
Who do you think you are?

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:35.759
You're nothin' but a court jester.

00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:38.520
What I wanna know is what you think of it.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:39.638
It's a bit of a jumble.

00:01:39.708 --> 00:01:42.199
A collection of fragments
that leap around in time

00:01:42.292 --> 00:01:43.360
like Mexican jumping beans.

00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:45.155
Welcome to my mind, old sock.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.357
Him, I get. But what did Marion
ever do to deserve this?

00:01:48.478 --> 00:01:50.160
It's not her!

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.440
Not all characters are headliners.
Some are secondary.

00:01:53.542 --> 00:01:56.117
You pick a fight with Willie,
you are finished.

00:01:56.208 --> 00:01:58.487
Mayer can't save you. Nobody can.

00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:00.500
Especially the boy genius from New York.

00:02:00.603 --> 00:02:03.918
I removed any distraction,
eliminated every excuse.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.799
Your family, your cronies, liquor.

00:02:06.598 --> 00:02:08.958
I gave you a second chance.

00:02:09.042 --> 00:02:12.680
You cannot capture
a man's entire life in two hours.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.117
All you can hope is to leave
the impression of one.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.838
Why Hearst?
Outside his own blonde Betty Boop,

00:02:18.917 --> 00:02:20.856
you were always
his favorite dinner partner.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.531
Are you familiar with the parable

00:02:23.614 --> 00:02:26.193
of the organ grinder's monkey?

